BraleModule_Execute
├── when the caller is not the PaymentRails
│   └── it should revert with BraleModule_NotPaymentRails
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Zero amount"
├── when params are shorter than 96 bytes
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when params use the old two-field encoding
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when minAmount is zero
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Zero minimum amount"
├── when amount is below minAmount
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Below minimum redemption"
├── when amount equals minAmount
│   └── it should succeed and move the amount
├── when params have dirty address bits
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when depositAddress is zero
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Zero deposit address"
├── when depositAddress is the PaymentRails
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Deposit address is PaymentRails"
├── when depositAddress is the module
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Deposit address is module"
├── when depositAddress is the input token
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Deposit address is input token"
├── when depositAddress is the output token
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Deposit address is output token"
├── when outputToken is zero
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Zero output token"
├── when outputToken equals the input token
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Output token equals input token"
├── when params are invalid
│   ├── it should leave the nonce unchanged
│   ├── it should not move tokens
│   └── it should not emit RedemptionInitiated
├── when the token transfer returns false
│   ├── it should return a failed result with "Token transfer failed"
│   └── it should restore the nonce
├── when the token transfer reverts
│   ├── it should return a failed result with "Token transfer failed"
│   └── it should restore the nonce
├── when the token charges a recipient fee
│   └── it should revert with BraleModule_UnexpectedDeliveredAmount
├── when the token charges a sender fee
│   └── it should revert with BraleModule_UnexpectedDebitedAmount
├── when the token reenters the PaymentRails during transfer
│   ├── it should return a failed result
│   └── it should leave the nonce unchanged
└── when params are valid
    ├── it should deliver exactly the amount to the deposit address
    ├── it should debit exactly the amount from the PaymentRails
    ├── it should leave the module balance at zero
    ├── it should emit RedemptionInitiated with the expected id
    ├── it should increment the nonce
    ├── it should return a success result carrying the redemption id
    ├── it should produce distinct ids for consecutive calls
    └── it should move the exact amount for any amount (fuzz)
